review:
TL;DR Fun addictive ARPG grindfest

Wot I liked
- Many classes, many skill trees many combinations of your abilities;
- Gearfest with many unique items to augent your build;
- Many ways for loot improvement: enchanting, transmuting , socketing, runes, etc.; 
- Perfect loot grinder - kill, loot, level up, sell trash, upgrade gear, repeat;
- Endgame: either short runs with bosses or randomised zones or endless mode. Kill, loot, upgrade; 
- You can change difficulties on the fly.

Wot I disliked
- It's too 2d;
- GUI positioning. Buffs are small (regardless of the UI scale) and are difficult to track;
- The game's combat is high speed and is centered around buffs and cds, so you mostly look at the corner of the screen to use the abilities when they are off cd;
- Stupid minimap that you have to resize 5 times to use;
- Combat is not really controllable. You just click mobs to death;
- Combat gets really repetetive. You can choose diffrent abilities but they mostly feel the same.

To sum it all up, it's a fun little action heavy ARPG looter grindfest. I wish the combat was a bit more appealing, slower and animations were not so 2D.
